Relocatable SPURS images: fixups for jobs with their CRT, and custom modules.

-mspurs-job-initialize links with --emit-fixups; its job runtime relocates the
image from the table.  New -mcustom-module builds a position-independent image
for a custom policy module to load: compiled -fpic (so the pic multilib is
used), linked at 0 (the default layout) with --emit-fixups and -q, and started
by crti.o, init_fixups.o and crtbegin.o.  init_fixups.o (libgcc, every
multilib) adds the load address to the listed words from _init, then runs the
.init_array constructors (such an image has no crt0); its .fini fragment runs
.fini_array.  Both modes accept run-time relocations unless -merror-reloc or
-mwarn-reloc is given.

